---
// Rung 3 of the SIP ladder (dd-002) - counting the Answer as rung 1, which is
// how Rahul counts them and therefore how they are numbered here: "What did you put in, and what did the
// market add?"
//
// Both moneys side by side rather than behind a toggle (dd-006). The difference
// between the two columns IS the lesson, and a lesson cannot be a mode - hiding
// half of a comparison behind a control turns it into a spot-the-difference
// puzzle.
//
// One prose voice, one size (dd-007).
//
// No new concept. Rung 2 established that prices rise and that only the gap
// matters; this shows what that does in rupees, and answers the question every
// saver eventually asks: of everything I end up with, how much did I actually
// provide?
---

<section id="rungSipFlow" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-4" aria-labelledby="rungSipFlowQ">
  <div class="card-premium rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">

    <div>
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.11em] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
        Next question
      </p>
      <h2 id="rungSipFlowQ" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 mt-1">
        How much of that is yours, and how much is the market's?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-2">
        Over <span id="sipFlowYears" class="font-medium text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">20</span> years,
        putting in <span id="sipFlowMonthly" class="font-medium text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">—</span> a month.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-2 px-2">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <caption class="sr-only">
          What you put in and what the market added, shown both in today's prices
          and as your statement will report it.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700">
            <th scope="col" class="text-left font-normal text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 pb-2"></th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-right pb-2 pl-4">
              <span class="block text-xs font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">What it is worth</span>
              <span class="block text-[11px] font-normal text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">in today's prices</span>
            </th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-right pb-2 pl-4">
              <span class="block text-xs font-semibold text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">What your statement says</span>
              <span class="block text-[11px] font-normal text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">the number on the screen</span>
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-navy-100 dark:divide-navy-800">
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-normal text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300 py-2.5">You put in</th>
            <td id="sipCellInReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellInNom" class="text-right tabular-nums text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-normal text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300 py-2.5">The market added</th>
            <td id="sipCellGrowthReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellGrowthNom" class="text-right tabular-nums text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-normal text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300 py-2.5">
              The fund takes
              <span id="sipCellFeeLabel" class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400"></span>
            </th>
            <td id="sipCellFeeReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellFeeNom" class="text-right tabular-nums text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
          <!-- The ledger lands twice: once before tax and once after. It used
               to land once and print "not counted yet" for tax whenever the
               page's BEFORE TAX button was in its shipped position — so the one
               screen whose job is to show where the money goes omitted the last
               thing that takes some (sol-037). Both landings are always shown,
               so this rung contains whichever figure the Answer is quoting and
               cannot contradict it. -->
          <tr class="border-t border-navy-300 dark:border-navy-600">
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200 py-2.5">
              Before tax you have
            </th>
            <td id="sipCellPreTaxReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellPreTaxNom" class="text-right tabular-nums text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-normal text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300 py-2.5">
              Tax takes, when you sell
              <span id="sipCellTaxLabel" class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400"></span>
            </th>
            <td id="sipCellTaxReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellTaxNom" class="text-right tabular-nums text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-2.5 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-t-2 border-navy-300 dark:border-navy-600">
            <th scope="row" class="text-left font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-3">
              So you keep
            </th>
            <td id="sipCellEndReal" class="text-right tabular-nums font-bold text-base text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 py-3 pl-4">—</td>
            <td id="sipCellEndNom" class="text-right tabular-nums font-semibold text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 py-3 pl-4">—</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- The one thing the two columns exist to show. -->
    <p id="sipFlowGap" class="rounded-lg bg-gold-500/10 border border-gold-500/30 px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200"></p>

    <!-- One idea, one voice, one size. -->
    <p id="sipFlowIdea" class="text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200"></p>

    <div class="pt-4 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
        All of which assumes the market delivers what we assumed it would.
        <span class="font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">What if it does not?</span>
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id);
  const grp = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-IN');

  function money(n: number): string {
    const v = Math.round(n);
    if (Math.abs(v) >= 10000000) return `₹${(v / 10000000).toFixed(2)} crore`;
    if (Math.abs(v) >= 100000) return `₹${(v / 100000).toFixed(1)} lakh`;
    return `₹${grp(v)}`;
  }

  function render(detail: any) {
    const { inputs, outlook, simulation } = detail;
    const f = outlook.flow;
    const years = inputs.horizonYears;

    $('sipFlowYears')!.textContent = String(years);
    $('sipFlowMonthly')!.textContent = `₹${grp(inputs.monthlySip)}`;

    // Every figure is the engine's; nothing here is re-derived (sol-023). Both
    // columns close: put in + market added − the fund's cut − tax = what you keep.
    $('sipCellInReal')!.textContent = money(f.investedReal);
    $('sipCellInNom')!.textContent = money(f.investedNominal);
    $('sipCellGrowthReal')!.textContent = money(f.growthReal);
    $('sipCellGrowthNom')!.textContent = money(f.growthNominal);
    // The fund's fee. It was invisible until today - not hidden, simply netted
    // off the growth, which is the same thing from where the reader sits.
    $('sipCellFeeReal')!.textContent = `− ${money(f.feeReal)}`;
    $('sipCellFeeNom')!.textContent = `− ${money(f.feeNominal)}`;
    $('sipCellFeeLabel')!.textContent =
      `${inputs.expenseRatio.toFixed(2)}% a year, every year`;
    // Always counted. "Not counted yet" was honest about the toggle and
    // dishonest about the money: a reader looking at a ledger is entitled to
    // see every line of it, and the tax is owed whether or not a button
    // upstairs is pressed (sol-037, dd-006).
    $('sipCellPreTaxReal')!.textContent = money(f.preTaxEndReal);
    $('sipCellPreTaxNom')!.textContent = money(f.preTaxEndNominal);
    $('sipCellTaxReal')!.textContent = `− ${money(f.taxAlwaysReal)}`;
    $('sipCellTaxNom')!.textContent = `− ${money(f.taxAlwaysNominal)}`;
    $('sipCellTaxLabel')!.textContent =
      `${inputs.ltcgTax}% on the gain, first ₹1.25 lakh exempt`;
    $('sipCellEndReal')!.textContent = money(f.afterTaxEndReal);
    $('sipCellEndNom')!.textContent = money(f.afterTaxEndNominal);

    // The gap between the columns, said plainly. This is the whole reason both
    // are on screen: the statement figure is the one the reader will see, and
    // it is not the one that matters.
    const shrink = f.afterTaxEndNominal > 0
      ? 1 - f.afterTaxEndReal / f.afterTaxEndNominal : 0;
    $('sipFlowGap')!.textContent =
      `The number on the screen at the end will be ${money(f.afterTaxEndNominal)}. What ` +
      `that will actually buy, in the prices you know today, is ` +
      `${money(f.afterTaxEndReal)} — about ${Math.round(shrink * 100)}% less. Both ` +
      `numbers are true; only the second one is a plan.`;

    // The multiple is the thing worth carrying away (dd-010): not the total,
    // but what each rupee genuinely given up came back as.
    const mult = f.investedReal > 0 ? f.afterTaxEndReal / f.investedReal : 0;
    const share = f.afterTaxEndReal > 0
      ? Math.min(1, f.investedReal / f.afterTaxEndReal) : 1;
    $('sipFlowIdea')!.textContent =
      `Of the ${money(f.afterTaxEndReal)} you keep, ${money(f.investedReal)} is money ` +
      `you provided and ${money(f.afterTaxEndReal - f.investedReal)} is what time did ` +
      `with it. Every rupee you really gave up came back as ${mult.toFixed(2)} — ` +
      `so about ${Math.round(share * 100)} paise in the rupee is yours and the ` +
      `other ${Math.round((1 - share) * 100)} is compounding. That ratio is what ` +
      `a longer horizon buys you, and it is why the second lever on the answer ` +
      `above is years rather than money.`;

    // Unused, but read deliberately: the engine result is here so that a future
    // row can be added from it rather than computed beside it.
    void simulation;
  }

  window.addEventListener('sip:result', (e) => render((e as CustomEvent).detail));
</script>
